### Table 4.

Clinical toolbox for estimation of blood loss during postpartum hemorrhage.

|Tool |Parameters |
| --- | --- |
|Severity of blood loss |Total EBV during pregnancy = booking maternal body.weight × 100 mL (eg, if the booking weight is 40 kg, then EBV = 40 × 100 = 4000 mL);  
If the EBL is 30% of EBV, major PPH (eg, if EBL is 1500, then 1500/4000 is >37.5%). |
|OSI |Pulse rate/SBP should be <0.9 after birth;If the OSI is >1, likelihood of major PPH requiring a blood transfusion (eg, if the pulse rate is 100/min and SBP is 90 mmHg, then OSI = 100/90 = 1.11, which is >1). |
|Rule of 30 \* |SBP decreases by >30 mmHg;  
Pulse rate increases by >30 beats;  
Respiratory rate increases to >30/min;  
Urine output decreases to <30 mL/h;  
Hematocrit (PCV) decreases by 30%. |

